    "result_text": "The full test suite passed (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures). AcceptanceBase is abstract and AuditLogCapture is a helper, so AcceptanceTest is the only runnable test class.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` in `ClinicServiceImpl.generateCustomerCode`:\n\n- **CITY3** \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of the owner's city\n- **LAST3** \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of the last name\n- **NNNN** \u2014 a **per-city** 4-digit zero-padded sequence, one more than the number of owners already in that city (previously it was a global count of all owners)\n\nThe method now takes both `city` and `lastName`, and the caller in `saveOwner` passes `owner.getCity()`.\n\n**Derived values:** The membership number in `OwnerMapper` is `owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + ...`, so it is built directly from `customerCode` and automatically rebuilds on the new format \u2014 no separate change needed. `membershipTier` derives from `namesakeCount`/`email`, not the customer code, so it's unaffected.\n\nThe acceptance test's regex `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}` now matches.",
